Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:48:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): jstack tree rows follow v0.1.7's sidebar, buttons
 in the Tab order and no ARIA tree

Upstream's sidebar stopped being an ARIA tree (#26690): its rows are buttons in the Tab
order, the list holds no roving tab stop, and the active row says aria-current. The jstack
rows were still treeitems at tabIndex -1, which Tab now skips, so they take upstream's
shape: native buttons or role="button" rows in the Tab order, aria-current for the open
row. Their tests drop SIDEBAR_TREE_PROPS, which upstream removed, give the project
fixtures upstream's new pinned and archived fields, and find rows by role button.
chatRouteCommands.test.ts, new upstream, pins the tree off for its cases and adds the
tree's own, which starts in the current project.
